//
// Library.Dispatch.ailang
// Compiler-selectable linking/output dispatcher.
// Location: Librarys/Compiler/Link/Library.Dispatch.ailang
// Import:   LibraryImport.Compiler.Link.Dispatch
//
// PURPOSE:
//   Single entry point the compiler calls to finalize an output artifact.
//   Branches on (Emit.os, Emit.target_kind) to route to the correct
//   per-OS emitter + per-binary-type linking strategy.
//
//   target_kind axis:
//     "exec"        — ET_EXEC (or ET_DYN) userspace binary.
//                     Linux: direct syscall emission via CSysDispatch (today's path).
//     "kmod"        — ET_REL kernel module object.
//                     Linux: PLT32 relocs against the ail_shim ABI.
//     "shared_lib"  — (future) ET_DYN with PLT for libc or foreign-API linking.
//
//   os axis (matches Emit.os from CEmitCoreArch):
//     "linux", "haiku", "macos", "windows"
//
// WIRING:
//   ailang_cli.ailang parses -kmod / (default exec) / future -shared flags
//   and sets Emit.target_kind before invoking Link_Dispatch.
//
// IMPORT MAP (by target):
//   linux + exec  -> LibraryImport.Compiler.Output.COutput                    (existing, unchanged)
//   linux + kmod  -> LibraryImport.Compiler.Link.OS.Linux.ELFKernelModule     (moved here)
//   linux + *     -> LibraryImport.Compiler.Link.OS.Linux.KernelABI           (syscall -> shim symbol map)
//   *   -> LibraryImport.Compiler.Link.Core.RelocTable
//   *   -> LibraryImport.Compiler.Link.Core.SymbolTable
//
// STATUS: Scaffold — Link_Dispatch body not yet wired. Existing CLI paths
// keep working until this file is brought online.

LibraryImport.Compiler.Link.Core.RelocTable
LibraryImport.Compiler.Link.Core.SymbolTable

